    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "For MyCorp, the process begins by entering expenses."
      ],
      "justification": "Initiates the process and executes the initial step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After entering expenses, the next step is to generate a spreadsheet."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct correspondence to the sequential generation step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the spreadsheet is generated, the request can be approved or disapproved."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the first approval check and opens the first XOR decision point."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "label:b1->c_loop",
        "guard:b1->c_loop"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the request is not approved, the process goes back to entering expenses."
      ],
      "justification": "Negative branch routing back to the loop convergence."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "label:b1->n5",
        "guard:b1->n5",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the request is approved, the expenses can be paid out."
      ],
      "justification": "Positive branch leading to the first payout action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The process then checks again if the request is approved or not."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the second approval check and opens the second XOR decision point."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "label:b2->c_loop",
        "guard:b2->c_loop"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If it is not approved, the process goes back to entering expenses."
      ],
      "justification": "Second negative branch routing back to the loop convergence."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "label:b2->n8",
        "guard:b2->n8",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "But if it is approved, the expenses can be paid out."
      ],
      "justification": "Second positive branch leading to the second payout action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "converge:c_loop"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the request is not approved, the process goes back to entering expenses.",
        "If it is not approved, the process goes back to entering expenses."
      ],
      "justification": "Structural join node representing the return path to expense entry from both failed approvals."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, after the expenses are paid out, the process comes to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Final termination step and end node."
    }
